{"id": "EUVD-2026-103752", "enisaUuid": "b7a21bc1-d6ed-39c9-b6fd-7652cb221dc2", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau: RCU-free the scheduler-containing nouveau_sched\n\nstruct nouveau_sched embeds a struct drm_gpu_scheduler (base).\nnouveau_sched_destroy() calls nouveau_sched_fini() (which does\ndrm_sched_fini(&sched->base)) and then frees the object with plain\nkfree(sched).\n\ndrm_sched_fence_get_timeline_name() returns fence->sched->name, and the\nscheduler fence keeps a .release callback so it is not ops-detached on\nsignalling.  A finished fence exported to userspace via drm_syncobj /\nsync_file therefore keeps pointing at &sched->base after nouveau_sched_destroy(),\nand a later get_timeline_name() -- reachable unprivileged through\nSYNC_IOC_FILE_INFO -- dereferences freed memory (KASAN slab-use-after-free\nread).\n\nPer the dma-fence lifetime contract the exporter must keep the data backing a\nsignalled fence alive for an RCU grace period.  Free the scheduler-containing\nobject with kfree_rcu() instead of kfree().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:17:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:52", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/40edf5eefc3fd94592a91d6eb074d4fc6f606c75", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/35151e9a8274174ccbb92e3b3ba7dc7a008dcada", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cd6e11b6ebe04a0a1f1435df561acada9eadc563", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f7eae6d8d768fabd6b59779ca7da79e02c74e113"], "aliases": ["GHSA-2689-7jhq-fvhw", "CVE-2026-98512"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d030006-f780-39e2-8d73-c39b73593ddd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "28e7e983-d6d7-3b23-ac25-8c7498825619", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f03a507b29e44a848f315c7240c19894dd8be4f <40edf5eefc3fd94592a91d6eb074d4fc6f606c75"}, {"id": "3a49f980-347a-3b35-8a06-f733c66ab974", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b580518-af74-33fb-8dc2-53040c7ceb29", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f03a507b29e44a848f315c7240c19894dd8be4f <f7eae6d8d768fabd6b59779ca7da79e02c74e113"}, {"id": "410d6ec7-72c8-33be-a1bd-05c01940771e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f03a507b29e44a848f315c7240c19894dd8be4f <35151e9a8274174ccbb92e3b3ba7dc7a008dcada"}, {"id": "6cfe8658-f413-358b-a077-538451cdf603", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5f03a507b29e44a848f315c7240c19894dd8be4f <cd6e11b6ebe04a0a1f1435df561acada9eadc563"}, {"id": "70acd66e-5803-33e9-ac40-d444b20956ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "76c6c5bf-8b85-33a8-b3a5-167c53b1c4ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "b4ec1aeb-f6cb-3e93-bf80-d316bc63d516", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "f660a0eb-f0e1-36b9-b084-a9f2e70f7c78", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3a6f8155-a1ec-381c-a20b-39d19755d4e0", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}